hi Latha,
fullfill your deepest desire: network programming, driver hacking etc.
the linux kernel has special maintainer for each (see: MAINTAINERS).

*Here* your are in the *janitors group*. we do the cleanup work that 
programmers tend to forget. like:
checking return codes propperly, fixing warning and documentation,...
i think this is good stuff for entring the kernel world.

beside this there are special interest groups like the 
linux-test-project and special hardware projects.

feel free to join us,
walter





